<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="Uninstalling-17CF135F" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Uninstalling</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">During the <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword ">Niagara</keyword> installation, the appropriate Uninstall executable
is copied to the !bin subfolder, and renamed to <filepath class="+ topic/ph sw-d/filepath ">uninstall.exe</filepath>. The installed <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Start</uicontrol> menu <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Uninstall</uicontrol> shortcut points to this executable.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">Uninstalling</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><context class="- topic/section task/context "><p class="- topic/p ">Running the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Uninstaller</uicontrol> removes
only the installation runtime files and folders in the niagara_home
location (<filepath class="+ topic/ph sw-d/filepath ">C:\Niagara\Niagara-4.11.xx.xx</filepath>). The files and folders located in your niagara_user
home (<filepath class="+ topic/ph sw-d/filepath "><text conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/user_home_workbench" class="- topic/text "/></filepath>) and in the platform daemon user home (<filepath class="+ topic/ph sw-d/filepath "><text conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/user_home_daemon" class="- topic/text "/></filepath>) are left untouched.</p><?Pub Caret 114?></context><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Under the Windows Start menu, click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">All Programs</uicontrol> and scroll to the <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword ">Niagara</keyword> build you wish to uninstall.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Click <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Niagara build</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Uninstall</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol "><wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Uninstall Program</wintitle></uicontrol> wizard opens.</stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Confirm that the wizard lists the correct build and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Next</uicontrol>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The wizard notifies you as it immediately begins uninstalling.</stepresult></step></steps><result class="- topic/section task/result ">On completion, the wizard notifies you that the uninstallation
is complete.</result></taskbody></task>